From cb4ac494b00a2dbcdfe0c7cf508e908db88d0663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:57:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): place managed workers in their run scope and
 bound the aggregate pool (#396)

* fix(kanban): place managed workers in their run scope and bound the aggregate pool

The real worker is a gateway Popen child, so it ran in the uncapped hermes-gateway.service
while only the ~50MB submitter sat in the per-run 8GiB scope. Several runs thrashed host
memory/IO (PSI full 40%, load 222) until worker_receipt_timeout tripped 12 cards.
Move the spawned child into the verified claim's scope (fail closed, kill+reap) and put all
run scopes in hermes-kanban.slice (MemoryHigh=70%, MemoryMax=80%). [daveey]

* fix(kanban): wait for submitter PID publication before verifying run scope
